{"t": 1794113325.3328555, "kind": "call", "tool": "gitlab_create_merge_request_thread", "args": {"body": "## Main pipeline is red \u2014 fix explained\n\n**Failure:** pipeline #8812 on `main` (sha `a91c2e0`) fails in job `test:contract` (`#77104`):\n\n```\nFAILED contract/test_invoice.py::test_invoice_number_format\nE  AssertionError: assert 'INV-2026-42' == 'INV-2026-000042'\n```\n\n**Root cause:** `billing/invoice.py::invoice_number()` built the number as `f\"INV-{year}-{seq}\"`, so the sequence was not padded. The finance contract for the ERP import (FIN-77) requires the sequence part to be zero-padded to 6 digits \u2014 the contract test asserts `invoice_number(2026, 42) == \"INV-2026-000042\"`.\n\n**Fix** (in `billing/invoice.py`):\n\n```python\ndef invoice_number(year: int, seq: int) -> str:\n    # Finance ERP import (FIN-77): sequence part is zero-padded to 6 digits.\n    return f\"INV-{year}-{seq:06d}\"\n```\n\n`06d` left-pads the sequence to 6 digits without truncating longer values (`123456` stays `123456`, `9999999` stays `9999999`), so this keeps the ERP v2 format consistent with the import contract.\n\n**Verification:** reproduced the contract assertions locally after the change:\n- `invoice_number(2026, 42)` -> `INV-2026-000042` \u2705\n- `invoice_number(2026, 1)` -> `INV-2026-000001` \u2705\n- `invoice_number(2026, 123456)` -> `INV-2026-123456` \u2705\n\nWith this change `test:contract` (and therefore the `main` pipeline) passes. Please rebase/merge this MR so the fix lands on `main`.", "merge_request_iid": "12", "project_id": "acme/billing-legacy"}, "ok": true}
